 Derived query -> A derived query is a query that Spring Data JPA automatically generates from the method name.
 @query -> @Query is an annotation in Spring Data JPA used to define custom JPQL or native SQL queries directly inside a repository interface.

 Spring Data JPA queries ko 2 tarike se handle karta hai: Derived Query aur @Query.


List<ProductsEntity> findByName(String name);


Tum method ka naam likhte ho, aur Spring Data JPA us naam ko parse karke automatically query banata hai.

findBy → data search karna

Name → entity ki name property

String name → search karne ke liye value

Agar tum "Laptop" pass karte ho, toh conceptually SQL aisi hogi:
You write the method name, and Spring Data JPA parses it to automatically generate the database query.



sql
SELECT * FROM products WHERE name = 'Laptop';
Behind the scenes: Spring Data JPA repository create hote waqt method name ko samajhta hai aur query generate karta hai. Tumhe manually SQL likhne ki zaroorat nahi hoti.

2. @Query ko kaise handle karta hai?

java
@Query("SELECT p FROM ProductsEntity p WHERE p.price > 1000")
List<ProductsEntity> findExpensiveProducts();
Ismein tum khud query likhte ho.

@Query Spring Data JPA ko batata hai ki is method ke liye custom query use karni hai.

ProductsEntity entity class hai.

p us entity ka alias hai.

p.price > 1000 condition hai.

Behind the scenes:

Spring Data JPA reads the query defined in @Query.

A JPA provider such as Hibernate translates JPQL into SQL.

The SQL query executes against the database.

The results are mapped into ProductsEntity objects and returned.



Derived Query                                             @Query

Query is generated from the method name.    You define the query yourself.
Example: findByName()                     Example: @Query("SELECT...")
Useful for simple queries.             Useful for custom or complex queries.






